-- ccc10-hate-crime.l4 -- section 320.1001 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: the offence of committing another offence motivated by hatred.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (every element holds, or the rule applies); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words, quoted in the branch's comment);
-- NOTHING (not covered: an element is missing, the text is silent or limits a prohibition in its own wording, or the answer points outside the text).
-- A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE. Seams: `s 319(7) ...` is answered by ccc10-hate.l4 (the definition of hatred; s 320.1001(2) points at it); `s 787(1) ...` is ccc29's.

§ `s 320.1001 -- Offence motivated by hatred`

DECLARE `s 320.1001(1) the ground of hatred` IS ONE OF
    `s 320.1001(1) race`
    `s 320.1001(1) national or ethnic origin`
    `s 320.1001(1) language`
    `s 320.1001(1) colour`
    `s 320.1001(1) religion`
    `s 320.1001(1) sex`
    `s 320.1001(1) age`
    `s 320.1001(1) mental or physical disability`
    `s 320.1001(1) sexual orientation`
    `s 320.1001(1) gender identity or expression`
    `s 320.1001(1) another ground`

-- 320.1001(1): an offence defined with an explicit "if": a failed "if" is JUST FALSE (fork F51); a missing included offence or a ground outside the list is NOTHING.
-- src:6136 | 320.1001 (1) Everyone who commits an offence — referred to in this section as the “included offence” — under this Act or any other Act of Parliament, if the commission of the included offence is motivated by hatred based on race, national or ethnic origin, language, colour, religion, sex, age, mental or physical disability, sexual orientation or gender identity or expression, is
-- src:6137 | (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to the punishment provided for in subsection (5); or
-- src:6138 | (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 320.1001(1) (src:6136-6138)
GIVEN `the person commits an offence under this Act or any other Act of Parliament, the included offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commission of the included offence is motivated by an emotion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 319(7) as to whether the emotion is hatred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `s 320.1001(1) the ground of hatred`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.1001(1) the person is guilty of the offence of committing an offence motivated by hatred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person commits an offence under this Act or any other Act of Parliament, the included offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone who commits an offence — referred to in this section as the “included offence” — under this Act or any other Act of Parliament"
        IF `the commission of the included offence is motivated by an emotion` AND (`the answer of s 319(7) as to whether the emotion is hatred` EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the emotion is hatred is s 319(7)'s and is not determined
        IF `the commission of the included offence is motivated by an emotion` AND (`the answer of s 319(7) as to whether the emotion is hatred` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (ground EQUALS `s 320.1001(1) another ground`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "hatred based on race, national or ethnic origin, language, colour, religion, sex, age, mental or physical disability, sexual orientation or gender identity or expression" is not closed by "only"
        IF `the commission of the included offence is motivated by an emotion` AND (`the answer of s 319(7) as to whether the emotion is hatred` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the commission of the included offence is motivated by hatred based on race, national or ethnic origin, language, colour, religion, sex, age, mental or physical disability, sexual orientation or gender identity or expression" (the commission is not motivated by hatred: a failed "if", F51)

@ref s 320.1001(1) (src:6136-6138)
`s 320.1001(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:6139 | Definition of hatred
-- src:6140 | (2) In this section, hatred has the same meaning as in subsection 319(7).
@ref s 320.1001(2) (src:6139-6140)
GIVEN `the answer of s 319(7) as to hatred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.1001(2) the emotion is hatred` MEANS `the answer of s 319(7) as to hatred`

-- src:6141 | Clarification
-- src:6142 | (3) For greater certainty, the commission of an offence under this Act or any other Act of Parliament is not, for the purposes of this section, motivated by hatred based on any of the factors mentioned in subsection (1) solely because it discredits, humiliates, hurts or offends.
@ref s 320.1001(3) (src:6141-6142)
GIVEN `the only reason the commission of the offence is said to be motivated by hatred is that it discredits, humiliates, hurts or offends` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.1001(3) the commission of the offence is motivated by hatred` MEANS
    IF `the only reason the commission of the offence is said to be motivated by hatred is that it discredits, humiliates, hurts or offends`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the commission of an offence under this Act or any other Act of Parliament is not, for the purposes of this section, motivated by hatred based on any of the factors mentioned in subsection (1) solely because it discredits, humiliates, hurts or offends"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "solely because it discredits, humiliates, hurts or offends"

-- 320.1001(4): a bar "if": it applies when the included offence is summary only; otherwise the bar is silent (NOTHING).
-- src:6143 | Limitation
-- src:6144 | (4) No proceedings shall be commenced under subsection (1) by way of indictment if the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of summary conviction proceedings.
@ref s 320.1001(4) (src:6143-6144)
GIVEN `the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of summary conviction proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.1001(4) proceedings under subsection (1) may not be commenced by way of indictment` MEANS
    IF `the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of summary conviction proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceedings shall be commenced under subsection (1) by way of indictment if the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of summary conviction proceedings"

-- 320.1001(5): the maximum by the included offence's maximum. A Length of time is compared as (years x 12 + months) x 31 + days, less one for "less a day":
-- two years 744, five years 1860, ten years 3720, fourteen years 5208; two years less a day is 743, which no paragraph covers.
-- src:6145 | Maximum penalty
-- src:6146 | (5) Everyone who is found guilty of an indictable offence under subsection (1) is liable to a term of imprisonment of not more than
-- src:6147 | (a) five years, if the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence is two years or more but less than five years;
-- src:6148 | (b) 10 years, if the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence is five years or more but less than 10 years;
-- src:6149 | (c) 14 years, if the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence is 10 years or more but less than 14 years; or
-- src:6150 | (d) life, if the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence is 14 years or more and up to imprisonment for life.
@ref s 320.1001(5) (src:6145-6150)
GIVEN `the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence` IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A MAYBE Imprisonment
`s 320.1001(5) the term of imprisonment the person is liable to is not more than` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence`
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the included offence states no maximum term of imprisonment, which no paragraph covers
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST `imprisonment for life`
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` `the term` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the key of the term` AT LEAST 5208 THEN JUST `imprisonment for life`
            IF `the key of the term` AT LEAST 3720 THEN JUST (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`)
            IF `the key of the term` AT LEAST 1860 THEN JUST (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)
            IF `the key of the term` AT LEAST 744 THEN JUST (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`)
            OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a maximum below two years is within none of paragraphs (a) to (d)
        WHERE
            `the key of the term` MEANS ((`the term`'s years TIMES 12 PLUS `the term`'s months) TIMES 31 PLUS `the term`'s days) MINUS (IF `the term`'s `less a day` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

@ref s 320.1001(5) (src:6145-6146)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `the answer of s 320.1001(5)` IS A MAYBE Imprisonment
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
`s 320.1001(1) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN
        CONSIDER `the answer of s 320.1001(5)`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (5) gives no maximum for this included offence
        WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, x, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:6151 | Applicable provisions
-- src:6152 | (6) Subject to paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) and subsections (4) and (5), any provision of this Act or any other Act of Parliament — including one in respect of procedure, orders or consequences — that would have been applicable in relation to the included offence applies in relation to an offence under subsection (1).
@ref s 320.1001(6) (src:6151-6152)
GIVEN `the provision would have been applicable in relation to the included offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is displaced by paragraph (1)(a) or (b) or subsection (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.1001(6) the provision applies in relation to the offence under subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the provision would have been applicable in relation to the included offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any provision of this Act or any other Act of Parliament ... that would have been applicable in relation to the included offence"
        IF `the provision is displaced by paragraph (1)(a) or (b) or subsection (4) or (5)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) and subsections (4) and (5)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
